<section class="v2-section v2-soft"><div class="v2-shell">
<div class="v2-section-head"><div><p class="v2-eyebrow">What you are handing over</p><h2>The research work.<br>Not your decision.</h2></div><p>You can use our local guides yourself. The service is for the work of tracing, matching, and explaining a property's actual file.</p></div>
<div class="v2-scope-grid">
<article><h3>One property, matched carefully.</h3><p>We compare address, parcel, dates, and reference numbers before treating documents as the same history. A similar street name is not a match.</p></article>
<article><h3>A visible search and request trail.</h3><p>The brief identifies sources checked, records available, unanswered requests, and referrals. You can distinguish “not found here” from “not yet checked.”</p></article>
<article><h3>Conclusions you can check.</h3><p>Each finding points to a document or source reference. A permit, invoice, inspection, and environmental letter keep their separate meanings.</p></article>
<article><h3>A handoff for the next decision.</h3><p>We prioritize the remaining request or professional question. You and your transaction team decide what to do; this is not approval to buy or a tank-free certificate.</p></article>
</div><p class="v2-fine">Founder-led beta, not a government office. The public sample shows the format, not a completed customer case. We confirm feasibility before accepting the research scope.</p>
